# Docker build context = the working tree minus everything listed here.
# Keep the context at ~3 MB: it is transferred to the daemon on every build and
# `deploy/deploy.py` mirrors the same selection when it uploads files over SFTP.
#
# IMPORTANT: a pattern without a slash only matches at the context root (Go
# filepath.Match semantics), so any rule that must bite at depth is repeated
# with a `**/` prefix.

# --- VCS / IDE / agent scratch ------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.idea
.pi
.claude
.workbuddy
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Local scratch artifacts --------------------------------------------------
# One generic rule instead of `_*.py`: the old rule let every `_remote_*.json[l]`
# through, i.e. 112.8 MB of production dumps per build (OPTIMIZATION_REVIEW #3).
_*
**/_*

# --- Python build / lint / test noise ----------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
coverage
htmlcov

# --- Runtime state (lives on the arena-game-runtime volume) -------------------
runtime
backups
map_memory.json
tactic_config.json
game_stats.json
tactic_log.jsonl
tactic_log.jsonl.*
battle_log.jsonl
battle_log.jsonl.*
tactic_play.log
tactic_play.log.*
*.log
*.lock
direct_debug.json
direct_play.log

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# --- Repo-only tooling: never needed inside the image -------------------------
deploy
tests
diagnose.py
direct_wrapper.py
fix_*.py
pyproject.toml
requirements-dev.txt
*.md

# --- Web console: source only, no local deps or build output -----------------
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/coverage
node_modules
nul
